AHS-010 — Information Flow

Document ID: AHS-010
Title: Information Flow
Version: 1.0.0-draft
Status: Draft

Architectural Views: Information, Process

1. Purpose

This specification defines the canonical information flow of the Atlas Engineering Cognition Framework (AECF).

It specifies how engineering information is acquired, transformed, enriched, preserved, and communicated throughout the Atlas architecture while maintaining semantic integrity, traceability, and explainability.

2. Scope

This specification defines:

Information artifacts
Information transformations
Information ownership
Information propagation
Information integrity
Information lifecycle

It does not define storage technologies, serialization formats, or communication protocols.

3. Canonical Definition

Information Flow is the governed movement and transformation of engineering information through the Atlas cognitive architecture while preserving its meaning, provenance, context, and integrity.

4. Information Principles

Atlas information SHALL:

Preserve semantic meaning.
Preserve traceability.
Preserve engineering context.
Preserve engineering intent.
Preserve applicable constraints.
Never lose provenance.
Never be modified without recording the transformation.
5. Canonical Information Artifacts

Atlas recognizes the following primary engineering artifacts.

Artifact	Produced By	Consumed By
Engineering Observation	Observation	Evidence
Engineering Evidence	Evidence	Understanding
Engineering Understanding	Understanding	Memory, Reasoning
Engineering Memory	Memory	Knowledge
Engineering Knowledge	Knowledge	Reasoning
Engineering Conclusions	Reasoning	Capability
Engineering Recommendations	Capability	Decision Support
Decision Support Artifact	Decision Support	Human / External System

These artifacts constitute the canonical information flow through Atlas.

