7. Information Ownership

Each engineering artifact SHALL have a single authoritative owner.

Artifact	Owner
Observation	Observation Service
Evidence	Evidence Service
Understanding	Understanding Service
Memory	Memory Service
Knowledge	Knowledge Service
Conclusions	Reasoning Service
Recommendations	Capability Service
Decision Support Artifact	Decision Support Service

Ownership defines responsibility for creation, validation, lifecycle management, and integrity.

8. Information Metadata

Every engineering artifact SHALL include the following metadata.

Identity

Globally unique identifier.

Source

Origin of the artifact.

Timestamp

Creation and modification timestamps.

Context

Engineering context applicable to the artifact.

Intent

Engineering objective associated with the artifact.

Constraints

Applicable engineering constraints.

Confidence

Current confidence assessment.

Traceability

Links to predecessor artifacts.

Explainability

References supporting engineering justification.

Version

Artifact version identifier.

9. Information Integrity

Atlas SHALL ensure:

No information corruption.
No silent modification.
Complete provenance.
Consistent semantic interpretation.
Deterministic transformations.
Versioned updates.

Integrity SHALL be verifiable throughout the information lifecycle.

