Every transition SHALL be traceable.

11. Information Exchange Rules

Information exchanged between services SHALL:

Use canonical engineering artifacts.
Preserve metadata.
Preserve traceability.
Preserve engineering semantics.
Preserve version compatibility.

Services SHALL reject artifacts that violate canonical integrity requirements.

12. Conformance

An implementation conforms if it:

Uses canonical engineering artifacts.
Preserves required metadata.
Maintains semantic integrity.
Maintains end-to-end traceability.
Documents all information transformations.
13. Future Evolution

Future revisions MAY introduce:

Additional artifact types.
Domain-specific engineering artifacts.
Semantic compression techniques.
Federated information models.
Digital twin information mappings.

Such additions SHALL remain consistent with the canonical information model.